-- Batch 07: traditional reference identity first; preserve modern observational content in existing astronomy sections.
-- Source-checked al-Bīrūnī Book of Instruction §347 and §§386–401, with source-specific exceptions.
-- Original interpretations, source tables, relations and formulas are not replaced.
PRAGMA foreign_keys=ON;

UPDATE terms SET short_definition='Jupiter is the greater benefic of the diurnal sect in traditional astrology, classified as moderately hot and moist. It rules Sagittarius and Pisces and is exalted in Cancer.',editorial_notes='Batch 07: traditional lexicographic headword priority, source-collated planetary nature.' WHERE slug='jupiter';
UPDATE terms SET short_definition='Mars is the lesser malefic of the nocturnal sect in traditional astrology, classed as extremely hot and dry by al-Bīrūnī. It rules Aries and Scorpio and is exalted in Capricorn.',editorial_notes='Batch 07: traditional lexicographic headword priority, source-collated planetary nature.' WHERE slug='mars';
UPDATE terms SET short_definition='Mercury rules Gemini and Virgo and signifies reasoning, speech and calculation in traditional astrology. Its benefic or malefic character and sect affinities depend on planetary company and authorial doctrine.',editorial_notes='Batch 07: traditional lexicographic headword priority, source-collated planetary nature.' WHERE slug='mercury';
UPDATE terms SET short_definition='The Moon is the principal luminary of the nocturnal sect, traditionally considered cold and moist, with a variable benefic or malefic character. It rules Cancer and is exalted in Taurus.',editorial_notes='Batch 07: traditional lexicographic headword priority, source-collated planetary nature.' WHERE slug='moon';
UPDATE terms SET short_definition='The Sun is the principal luminary of the diurnal sect, traditionally classed as hot and dry. It rules Leo and is exalted in Aries, and determines the chart''s day or night sect by its horizon position.',editorial_notes='Batch 07: traditional lexicographic headword priority, source-collated planetary nature.' WHERE slug='sun';
UPDATE terms SET short_definition='Venus is the lesser benefic of the nocturnal sect, described by al-Bīrūnī as moderately cold and moist. It rules Taurus and Libra and is exalted in Pisces.',editorial_notes='Batch 07: traditional lexicographic headword priority, source-collated planetary nature.' WHERE slug='venus';

